From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: an element's filter objects (element.filters) (9603)

In Internet Explorer's legacy document modes scripts read and change
visual filters through element.filters: filters.alpha.opacity = 50,
filters.item("DXImageTransform.Microsoft.Alpha"), filters[0], and
transitions' apply()/play(). The collection was always empty, so those
scripts threw. The element's filter list (what a script set in
style.filter, else the style attribute) is now the collection: a filter
object reads its parameters from the list (numbers, booleans, strings,
documented defaults such as Alpha's opacity 100) and writing one writes
the list back through style.filter. Transitions finish at once (no
animation). style.filter's rendering now takes
progid:DXImageTransform.Microsoft.Alpha(Opacity=..) and any case, as
alpha(opacity=..) before.
---
